<title>USA: Rock Bottom sees Q3 restructuring charges.</title>
<headline>Rock Bottom sees Q3 restructuring charges.</headline>
<dateline>LOUISVILLE, Colo. 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rock Bottom Restaurants Inc said Monday it expects to post charges of between about $3 million and $5 million in the third quarter related to restructuring plans.</p>
<p>The company said it plans to write down some longtime restaurant assets to fair market value and to streamline its headquarters operations.</p>
<p>The majority of the restructuring charges will be non-cash, it said. However, Rock Bottom said it anticipates achieving possible savings in future general and administrative expenses as a result of the restructuring.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
